hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.17.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * TheAudioDB answers the Song cover art method, alongside Last.fm. The two
    cover different ground -- for the radio track that prompted this work
    TheAudioDB knows nothing and Last.fm has a 1200x1200 cover, while for a
    well-known album track both answer -- and the cover art manager grades and
    sorts whatever comes back, so having both is worth more than either.
  * A track TheAudioDB has no picture of falls back to the cover of the album
    its own answer names. It knows many more tracks than it holds pictures of:
    of five well-known tracks sampled, three carried no track image, but all
    five named their album. Without the fallback the provider would miss most
    of what it actually knows. This is the album art for the song being played,
    and the same thing the Last.fm song provider returns.
  * Track lookups are cached both ways, as artist and album lookups already
    were, so a track TheAudioDB does not know is asked about once rather than
    on every play.

